WEBVTT

00:01.440 --> 00:06.820
The date for the All-Student Praxis
has been decided, Lord Cariot.

00:06.820 --> 00:10.360
There's no need to report
every little detail, Logwell.

00:10.360 --> 00:14.370
I don't exactly like to be the representative
of the Vanders, even if it's only temporary.

00:14.370 --> 00:16.540
The Thunder Faction is indulgent,

00:16.540 --> 00:18.330
the Elf Faction is prideful,

00:18.330 --> 00:20.170
and the Ice Faction is indolent.

00:20.880 --> 00:26.880
There's no one better suited for the position
than you, Vander of Incindia Barham.

00:29.410 --> 00:33.010
INCINDIA BARHAM - CARIOT INCINDIA WISEMAN
Has our king still not returned?

00:33.010 --> 00:35.520
AIDE-DE-CAMP OF FIRE FACTION - LOGWELL
He has not yet returned from the expedition.

00:36.600 --> 00:38.270
Good grief.

00:39.020 --> 00:42.130
Even though this barrier is already
on the verge of disappearing...

00:44.610 --> 00:48.480
Let the All-Student Praxis begin!

00:57.620 --> 01:01.420
I'll get results here
and definitely go to where Elfie is.

01:01.830 --> 01:03.330
Wignall, you're up.

01:03.330 --> 01:03.790
Huh?

01:05.170 --> 01:06.090
Mellvent.

01:19.430 --> 01:20.810
Shall we go?

01:21.160 --> 01:22.270
Are you okay?

01:22.270 --> 01:23.270
Ouch...

01:26.980 --> 01:29.440
That's Crimson Ant!

01:30.980 --> 01:32.240
And a swarm of them!

01:32.240 --> 01:33.450
All of a sudden?!

01:33.830 --> 01:36.410
Mages are at their weakest
in close combat.

01:36.410 --> 01:38.450
I'll have to be in front
and be their shield.

01:38.450 --> 01:39.790
No need.

01:40.870 --> 01:42.500
Lihanna Owenzaus.

01:43.210 --> 01:47.710
Don't you know what her family
is known for?

01:51.590 --> 01:55.600
Roar, O thunder spirits,
as I face my foe.

01:56.640 --> 01:57.850
Owen Sique...

01:59.390 --> 02:00.600
Lisolde Dua!

02:02.060 --> 02:03.270
Enchantment...

02:04.020 --> 02:06.730
The Owenzaus is a family of knights.

02:07.230 --> 02:12.990
Lihanna is a rare kind of mage
who specializes in close-combat magic.

02:17.080 --> 02:19.870
Competing with the others for credits
would be troublesome.

02:20.620 --> 02:23.120
We have to get ahead of all
the other parties quickly.

02:23.540 --> 02:24.770
Let's go.

03:48.120 --> 03:51.380
EPISODE 9: LET THE PRAXIS BEGIN

03:56.670 --> 04:00.720
Do you know what the most important
spell in the dungeon, Will?

04:01.910 --> 04:05.560
Is it an attack spell? Defense spell?
Neither.

04:06.770 --> 04:08.560
The answer is Search.

04:08.560 --> 04:12.770
A common spell used to detect
enemies and anomalies.

04:13.480 --> 04:18.550
For mages who are diving through dungeons,
it's the most basic and important spell.

04:25.950 --> 04:27.660
You're in the way, Flunkee!

04:28.130 --> 04:29.830
I can't locate the enemies in time.

04:29.830 --> 04:34.670
No, their Search range is wider
than my detection.

04:35.170 --> 04:40.430
If this keeps on, they'll sweep the enemies
before I can even engage.

04:41.090 --> 04:42.510
Finally got one.

04:42.510 --> 04:44.150
Zephros Claw.

04:49.060 --> 04:52.990
He got them all with one spell.

04:53.810 --> 04:56.480
You're more dead weight
than I expected.

04:56.480 --> 04:58.780
You can't even serve as a shield.

04:59.280 --> 05:04.080
This makes me question
your judgment, Lihanna.

05:05.030 --> 05:07.950
He simply hasn't had time
to be a shield yet.

05:08.540 --> 05:12.710
He'll show what his worth is
when we're up against Five-Over Enemies.

05:12.710 --> 05:13.670
Probably.

05:14.420 --> 05:16.670
That's why it's fine
if he's a dead weight now.

05:16.670 --> 05:18.070
Probably.

05:18.070 --> 05:19.470
He's definitely strong.

05:19.860 --> 05:21.220
Probably.

05:21.760 --> 05:23.470
I warned you, didn't I?

05:23.880 --> 05:27.210
Those who can't use Search
would only slow us down.

05:29.730 --> 05:35.230
Mages can absorb magical traces
into their wands.

05:35.720 --> 05:38.820
This way, the wand stores
a record of the battle.

05:38.820 --> 05:44.070
So the academy can verify
the monsters and the credits.

05:44.650 --> 05:48.040
Wait a minute!
He's still picking up item drops.

05:48.040 --> 05:52.540
What's the point in carrying
that hardly worth anything back with us?

05:52.540 --> 05:55.130
Sorry! It's all done.

05:55.130 --> 05:59.010
That's why, someone who can't
absorb the traces like me

05:59.010 --> 06:02.380
need to pick the drops to get credits.

06:02.380 --> 06:04.640
As a result, people hate
forming parties with me.

06:05.090 --> 06:08.640
You could at least try to be less pathetic
now that you're with us, Flunkee.

06:10.230 --> 06:11.860
Are you okay, Will?

06:13.980 --> 06:16.650
I already knew this was going to happen.

06:17.520 --> 06:21.530
So I'll do my best to help everyone
in other ways.

06:22.360 --> 06:24.320
That's what I said, but...

06:28.780 --> 06:30.910
There's nothing I can do.

06:31.450 --> 06:34.040
I already expected this, but...

06:34.470 --> 06:37.540
They're so outstanding.
No chance for me to show off.

06:37.540 --> 06:41.160
At this rate, I'm really going to be
no more than a baggage carrier.

06:43.010 --> 06:46.340
It's been a day since the praxis started.

06:46.340 --> 06:48.300
It's time we take a rest.

06:48.300 --> 06:50.430
Right here?

06:50.430 --> 06:55.980
I'm not asking for a high-class inn,
but I would like some security.

06:55.980 --> 06:59.190
Then, allow me to build
a fortress of flames.

06:59.770 --> 07:00.940
Nardrea.

07:04.070 --> 07:07.700
Wow! Is this Elven illusion magic?

07:07.700 --> 07:09.950
Yeah, I think so.

07:09.950 --> 07:12.580
The flames are just an illusion.

07:13.080 --> 07:17.260
But seeing flames pop out of nowhere
will make the monsters wary.

07:17.790 --> 07:19.090
They won't come near us.

07:19.710 --> 07:24.090
Serfort, pass out the rations
I gave you to everyone.

07:24.090 --> 07:25.590
Okay.

07:27.550 --> 07:29.350
Here's yours, Julius.

07:29.350 --> 07:30.800
Here's yours, Sion.

07:31.720 --> 07:33.720
And this yours, Wignall.

07:33.720 --> 07:36.730
Don't come any closer,
just leave it on the ground.

07:36.730 --> 07:37.520
Huh?

07:37.520 --> 07:40.610
Elves only allow people they
deem worthy to touch them.

07:41.190 --> 07:43.610
I'm sorry, but I don't want to
touch you by accident.

07:43.610 --> 07:47.490
Hey! We're all in the same party.
That's no way to talk to your teammates.

07:47.490 --> 07:51.370
You're mages. I'm an elf.

07:51.370 --> 07:57.250
Just give up, the only one that
I've deemed worthy here is Lihanna.

07:58.580 --> 08:00.540
Let's not fight, Colette.

08:00.540 --> 08:01.590
But...

08:01.590 --> 08:04.880
It's fine. Elves have their own
culture and customs.

08:05.590 --> 08:07.090
It doesn't bother me.

08:08.470 --> 08:13.100
Elves came here from
another world like Dwarves.

08:13.100 --> 08:15.770
But unlike them,
they're a magical race.

08:16.310 --> 08:17.890
They're Magic Users.

08:18.440 --> 08:21.480
They tend to stick to their own race,
and are snobbish.

08:22.020 --> 08:25.400
However, they indeed possess
more talent than most mages.

08:26.440 --> 08:31.820
Even one of the Magia Vander is
none other than the Elven Queen.

08:37.580 --> 08:39.790
Let's go over the plan.

08:43.750 --> 08:47.380
Our number one priority is
to defeat the Luminous Naberus.

08:47.380 --> 08:49.220
It's worth 110 credits.

08:49.220 --> 08:53.680
It's the only one of its kind,
the floor keeper for the 10th floor.

08:53.680 --> 08:55.060
110 credits!

08:55.060 --> 08:57.560
That's the most credits
you can get in a praxis.

08:57.560 --> 09:00.810
I've heard it's not rare for someone
to get killed taking on it.

09:01.400 --> 09:04.440
It's without a doubt,
the boss of the All-Student Praxis.

09:04.920 --> 09:09.700
You could say that I assembled
this party to take down Naberus.

09:10.110 --> 09:13.950
We have the ability to defeat
a monster worth 110 credits.

09:13.950 --> 09:15.890
I want to show this to the Tower.

09:16.540 --> 09:20.160
Now I'm here, so I don't intend
to turn back halfway.

09:20.830 --> 09:26.090
But is it all right to skip the appetizers
and jump straight to the main course?

09:26.090 --> 09:29.630
I want us to save our magic
so we're in the best shape possible.

09:29.630 --> 09:31.550
We can hunt other monsters for later.

09:32.550 --> 09:36.430
If there are no objections, let's take
the shortest route to the 10th floor.

09:37.520 --> 09:40.230
I've only earned five credits today.

09:40.810 --> 09:42.850
This won't do.

09:42.850 --> 09:45.210
To beat a floor keeper...

09:45.730 --> 09:48.070
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't scared.

09:48.820 --> 09:50.580
I'm going to do it, Elfie.

09:55.370 --> 09:58.370
Hey, what are you doing, Headless?

09:58.760 --> 10:01.660
Did you kill those guys upstairs?

10:05.330 --> 10:07.290
They were getting annoying.

10:07.290 --> 10:08.340
Huh?

10:08.750 --> 10:11.510
So I gave them Hell.

10:23.640 --> 10:25.230
What's going on here?

10:25.600 --> 10:29.480
I keep seeing monsters' corpses
everywhere.

10:30.730 --> 10:32.030
Did another party do this?

10:32.030 --> 10:32.950
THE DUNGEON 10TH FLOOR
Did another party do this?

10:32.950 --> 10:35.560
THE DUNGEON 10TH FLOOR
No, that's impossible.

10:35.560 --> 10:39.030
We took the fastest route
and we didn't stop at any base camps.

10:39.700 --> 10:43.540
No student could have
made it here before us.

10:44.920 --> 10:47.000
What are you doing, Will?

10:47.630 --> 10:50.130
There's no sign of magic used.

10:50.130 --> 10:52.880
They were torn apart by brute force.

10:53.670 --> 10:57.090
Naberus' room is just up ahead.

11:08.020 --> 11:11.260
The dungeon is unbelievably quiet.

11:13.150 --> 11:14.030
Could it be...

11:19.780 --> 11:20.910
Use Search!

11:22.660 --> 11:23.790
What's the meaning of this?

11:24.200 --> 11:25.920
There are still some traces here.

11:25.920 --> 11:27.540
It was killed just a while ago.

11:27.540 --> 11:29.670
You mean somebody slaughtered
the floor keeper?

11:29.670 --> 11:31.420
But who could have done this?

11:32.460 --> 11:34.170
Search is indeed very useful.

11:34.580 --> 11:36.380
But it isn't omnipotent.

11:36.380 --> 11:38.970
It can have a hard time
detecting crafty traps,

11:38.970 --> 11:42.930
and Mages can use the magic
"Hide" to counter it.

11:43.960 --> 11:48.560
And then, some monsters can
escape detection from Search.

12:01.910 --> 12:03.700
Everyone, above us!

12:07.540 --> 12:08.540
Will!

12:12.130 --> 12:13.300
What's happening?

12:19.220 --> 12:20.180
Wignall!

12:25.180 --> 12:26.020
Crims—

12:26.020 --> 12:26.770
Glace—

12:26.770 --> 12:27.430
Stia—

12:27.430 --> 12:28.270
Sagius—

12:52.000 --> 12:54.090
What is this quake?

12:55.210 --> 12:55.960
Will...

13:07.850 --> 13:09.600
Sorry.

13:10.980 --> 13:12.020
His arm...

13:14.570 --> 13:17.480
We fell down from the 10th floor.

13:17.480 --> 13:19.280
We're outside the Academy's territory.

13:20.740 --> 13:22.240
Did you say 11th floor?!

13:22.240 --> 13:25.870
You knew that we fell
from the 10th floor!

13:26.290 --> 13:28.750
This is ridiculous.
You must be joking!

13:28.750 --> 13:31.250
11th floor onwards is
the Tower's territory.

13:31.250 --> 13:35.130
Danger zones that only
High Mages can survive.

13:40.920 --> 13:42.550
The Nightmare's Maw.

13:43.050 --> 13:46.030
A vast region extending
all the way to the 15th floor.

13:46.030 --> 13:49.020
Both the structure of the labyrinth
and the power of the monsters

13:49.020 --> 13:52.690
are distinctly different from
the previous floors.

13:52.690 --> 13:54.270
Lihanna, you are bleeding!

13:54.980 --> 13:56.320
It's fine.

13:56.320 --> 13:59.150
I was hit by a rock when we fell.

13:59.150 --> 14:02.280
There's no one else around here.

14:02.710 --> 14:05.660
It's dangerous if we keep separated
from others on this 11th floor.

14:06.410 --> 14:11.160
We have to regroup quickly
or the dungeon will kill us.

14:11.660 --> 14:14.500
We, including Serfort and others,
could die.

14:29.040 --> 14:32.430
Wasting away in a school for mages.

14:32.430 --> 14:36.440
You can't even produce
a decent illusion.

14:36.440 --> 14:37.940
Have some shame!

14:39.940 --> 14:45.070
We have no need of a disgrace to our kin.

14:45.070 --> 14:47.320
Wait... Wait!

14:47.740 --> 14:49.580
There's no need...

14:49.580 --> 14:50.580
Ellenor!

14:50.580 --> 14:52.080
...for that useless arm either.

15:04.470 --> 15:06.430
Where am I?

15:06.430 --> 15:07.890
I'm glad you're awake.

15:07.890 --> 15:10.230
- Did he defeat this monster alone?
- Sorry, I haven't had a chance to treat you.

15:10.230 --> 15:11.520
Let's have some first aid now.

15:13.680 --> 15:15.100
Don't touch me!

15:16.940 --> 15:18.650
I'm an elf.

15:19.060 --> 15:21.010
Keep your hands off, No-talent!

15:21.650 --> 15:25.320
I don't care if you hate me
or you try to kill me someday,

15:25.320 --> 15:27.280
but I can't just leave you like that.

15:27.280 --> 15:29.530
Please, let me treat your arm.

15:30.330 --> 15:33.030
I can do it myself.

15:33.870 --> 15:35.120
Bring me the supplies!

15:40.950 --> 15:42.500
Wignall is injured.

15:43.090 --> 15:47.250
Our baggage including the medic kit
has also been wrecked.

15:48.050 --> 15:52.060
Including Rosty's magic items,
I've got three sub-weapons.

15:52.810 --> 15:54.930
We still have food and water.

15:55.450 --> 15:58.850
Colette and the others should
have their own pack.

15:58.850 --> 16:00.440
We should have enough for two days.

16:00.440 --> 16:01.770
No.

16:01.770 --> 16:04.610
We're on the 11th floor,
and under extreme conditions like this,

16:04.610 --> 16:06.490
we only have a day, at most.

16:06.490 --> 16:10.410
Our time limit is twenty-four hours.

16:12.030 --> 16:12.990
Wignall.

16:14.580 --> 16:16.910
We have to find Colette and the others.

16:17.410 --> 16:20.710
But that'll mean wandering around
the labyrinth, are you up to it?

16:20.710 --> 16:25.340
When we get stranded in the dungeon,
the protocol is to wait for rescue.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.670
But if you do nothing, you die.

16:28.260 --> 16:31.050
I believe that's how things work
in the dungeon.

16:31.850 --> 16:32.970
Moreover...

16:33.600 --> 16:38.210
So long as that monster is on the 10th floor,
any kind of rescue will be too late.

16:40.730 --> 16:43.730
What's going on there, Professor Eliza?

16:49.070 --> 16:49.860
It's a stampede, Workner.

16:49.860 --> 16:51.370
THE DUNGEON 8TH FLOOR - BASE CAMP
It's a stampede, Workner.

16:51.370 --> 16:53.330
THE DUNGEON 8TH FLOOR - BASE CAMP
The base camp was ravaged

16:53.330 --> 16:55.160
by rampaging monsters.

16:55.160 --> 16:58.020
Ravaged?!
What about Bruno and the others?

17:02.580 --> 17:04.000
They were killed.

17:04.590 --> 17:06.990
Something ripped their heads off.

17:09.420 --> 17:12.550
All our Masers other than this
have been crushed.

17:12.550 --> 17:15.260
I haven't heard from
the 9th floor or below,

17:15.260 --> 17:19.890
but I suspect the things there
are just as bad here.

17:21.060 --> 17:25.570
Not only a stampede, but the Academy
professors were murdered.

17:25.570 --> 17:27.280
This can't be a coincidence.

17:27.940 --> 17:29.490
Was this orchestrated by someone?

17:30.200 --> 17:31.740
What is going on really?

17:32.320 --> 17:35.330
Workner!
The All-Student Praxis is canceled!

17:35.770 --> 17:37.080
Professor Edward!

17:37.080 --> 17:39.450
This irregularity is putting
the students in danger!

17:39.450 --> 17:41.080
We're going to help them!

17:41.080 --> 17:42.500
Yeah!

18:03.810 --> 18:07.320
Wignall, you should try not to
use Search too much.

18:07.770 --> 18:11.640
Even if it's just a common spell,
if you abuse it, you'll use up all your magic.

18:11.640 --> 18:13.410
Right now, you should save your magic—

18:13.410 --> 18:14.610
Shut up!

18:14.610 --> 18:17.660
What if there's another ambush
like before?

18:17.660 --> 18:20.870
This is the 11th floor.
We shouldn't lower our guard.

18:20.870 --> 18:23.370
How can I afford to relax
in the middle of a danger zone?

18:23.830 --> 18:26.500
What matters for Search
is distance, not time.

18:27.210 --> 18:28.840
It depends on your range,

18:28.840 --> 18:31.740
but at the very least,
it should be used at 140 mille intervals.

18:31.740 --> 18:34.190
My range is about 70 selle.

18:34.800 --> 18:39.170
I'll let you know if we've taken 200 steps,
I'd like you to use Search during that time.

18:39.810 --> 18:42.120
Our detection range is different,

18:42.120 --> 18:45.150
so I want us to be more efficient
by dividing up our roles.

18:45.610 --> 18:48.360
Leave the detection of enemies
to Kiki and me.

18:48.360 --> 18:51.720
We'll definitely shut down
any ambushes.

18:53.150 --> 18:55.950
I want you to be on the lookout
for distant enemies.

18:55.950 --> 18:58.410
So we can avoid running
into any hordes.

18:58.410 --> 19:01.620
Instead of worrying about ambushes,

19:01.620 --> 19:04.960
right now we need to avoid fighting
as much as possible.

19:05.500 --> 19:06.920
I don't understand.

19:06.920 --> 19:11.170
How can you be so calm
at a time like this?

19:13.050 --> 19:18.180
If I want to climb the Tower,
my only choice is to get credits from praxis.

19:18.570 --> 19:22.430
I researched everything about the dungeon
and tried everything I could think of.

19:22.430 --> 19:24.640
It's not exactly something to be praised,

19:24.640 --> 19:27.560
but I've been stranded
about a hundred times.

19:28.230 --> 19:32.360
I have more experience,
at least a little more than you.

19:32.940 --> 19:34.820
That's all.

19:38.320 --> 19:39.130
They're coming.

19:52.460 --> 19:54.800
GERGESA - 8 CREDITS
The swine demon, Gergesa.

19:55.320 --> 19:57.760
I can sense more on the other route.

19:58.260 --> 20:00.180
Fighting is our only choice.

20:00.180 --> 20:01.680
I'll get the ones in front.

20:01.680 --> 20:03.820
Wignall, you take the one behind.

20:06.480 --> 20:07.810
O arrowhead, pierce through!

20:07.810 --> 20:09.310
Verdes Lana!

20:23.660 --> 20:27.000
How can he move like that?

20:27.000 --> 20:29.370
How can he fight in this situation?

20:29.880 --> 20:33.500
He managed to turn knowledge into wisdom,
and to know the unknown.

20:34.130 --> 20:36.550
Is that how he became so strong?

20:37.970 --> 20:39.840
Compared to him, I am...

20:41.640 --> 20:42.880
I'm just...

20:44.970 --> 20:45.640
Crap!

20:45.640 --> 20:47.730
No time to cast a counterattack spell!

20:47.730 --> 20:50.020
I'll use illusion to buy myself some time.

20:50.900 --> 20:52.110
Nardrea!

20:53.730 --> 20:54.690
Don't!

20:55.230 --> 20:56.780
Don't do it, Wignall!

20:57.570 --> 20:59.200
It won't work!

21:22.640 --> 21:23.510
Are you okay?

21:24.430 --> 21:28.310
Gergesas don't have eyes,
but they have a good sense of smell.

21:28.310 --> 21:30.690
So illusions won't work on them.

21:39.070 --> 21:41.140
What a disgrace.

21:42.160 --> 21:45.530
Don't let it get you down.
You're a talented elf.

21:45.530 --> 21:46.870
You'll get them next time.

21:46.870 --> 21:48.250
No.

21:48.250 --> 21:49.960
You're wrong.

21:51.460 --> 21:53.180
I'm not talented.

21:55.880 --> 21:56.950
I'm...

21:58.060 --> 22:00.040
...a flunkee.

23:36.640 --> 23:40.230
Next up, Episode 10 of
Wistoria: Wand and Sword,

23:40.940 --> 23:42.530
"Our Dreams."
